# speepobox-template: image/inputs v2 sha256:250e7d21ead1
# The files this repo's agent image is built from, beyond the Dockerfile.
# `speepobox image build` hashes them into the image's labels, and `doctor`
# recomputes that digest to tell whether the image is stale.
#
# One exact repo-relative path per line. No globs. Blank lines and `#`
# comments are ignored, and a listed path that does not exist refuses the
# build. The Dockerfile beside this file is always an input and is not listed.
#
# An image that bakes in its dependencies lists the manifest they come from,
# for example:
#
# package-lock.json
#
# This one lists nothing, because this image bakes in no dependency manifest:
# `node_modules/` arrives at run time through setup-hook.sh, into the
# bind-mounted checkout. Listing package-lock.json would therefore put an
# uncleanable stale warning on the image after every dependency bump — the T30
# failure in a new costume. setup-hook.sh is not an input either: it is
# mounted at run time, never copied into the image.
